  "visualReview": {
    "coverage": "Viewed every page and cover in eight 3×3 contact sheets, then re-viewed every corrected sheet. Full-size final checks: 0161 p07, 0164 p07, 0165 p06 and p08, 0166 p06, 0167 p06, 0168 p05 and p06.",
    "notes": [
      "0161: seal keeps the white knit cap and blue coat; completely white salt shell first shows one grey dot, then one curved stripe, then exactly three stripes. The clean stone is supported by a drying cloth and ends uncovered in a windowsill dish overlooking boats.",
      "0162: cloud keeps the blue vest and green mail bag; the empty mailbox contains only one yellow leaf, a self-written letter precedes the friend’s green envelope with one bent cucumber mark; the beetle has a red cap and brings one cucumber; final sunset resembles a carrot.",
      "0163: cloth bag keeps two brown buttons, waist buttonholes, two cloth feet and blue wheat embroidery. Two breads are loaded through the opening, straw fails, upper fabric folds, and buttons fasten the short bag; only one button is opened for the final two breads.",
      "0164: cloud horse has four short legs, grey mane, rounded ears and no wings. Lowered and standing body states are distinct; the rider has two arms, white socks, brown shoes and a yellow bag. Crossing uses a broad bridge with stone railing, and white lilies appear at the destination.",
      "0165: the spoon preserves its full handle length and blue end bow; horizontal ends reach opposite door jambs, then a diagonal head-first orientation passes into the opening. Face orientation remains readable. The finale places the spoon head within the porridge behind the front rim, with pink swirls visible.",
      "0166: purple curls and shell clip remain consistent. Both early plates have visible cinnamon speckles, while the replacement pear plate is plain. The old seasoned plate is set aside, the cinnamon jar is capped beside the host, and the final active plates remain one seasoned and one plain.",
      "0167: the windmill has exactly four alternating red/white blades. Exactly three wrappers are airborne or gathered; the transfer page has two in the box and the third between the hands. The sealed box leaves a clear flower bed, and next day the open box is visibly empty.",
      "0168: leaf child has exactly two head leaves; the paper bag retains its folded mouth and loose bottom corner. Seeds pour through the opened mouth into a wooden bowl; the bag lies flat with its bottom weighted by a board while glue dries. The filled bag enters the basket; after planting, an empty flattened bag remains in the basket."
    ],
    "limits": "Simplified vector picture-book style. Contact sheets inspect composition and continuity; selected pages enlarged. No claim of bitmap painting, audio QA, browser layout QA or child-user testing."
  },
